    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36322" root="قهب" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْهَبُ</span></b> , and its fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَهْبَآءُ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَهْبٌ</span>, first sentence,
in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَقْهَبَانِ</span> means <i>The elephant
and the buffalo:</i> (S, A, O, K:) each of them is
termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَقْهَبُ</span> because of his colour, (O, TA,) or
because of his greatness. (A, TA.)

